  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs#impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[outgoing_edges]` is appropriate.\n\n- **Form:** It is a fenced citation with commentary on an explicitly declared function that has a body. The built-in text allows that form, and it asks for a prose reason why incomplete coverage is acceptable.\n- **Substance:** The reason is substantive. The body is a deliberate `panic!(\"storage operations must not discover graph edges\")` guard, so it should never run in the storage tests.\n- **Agreement with current source:**\n  - The commentary says `Domain` requires this callback. This is true: the `Domain` trait in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs` declares `outgoing_edges` as a required method with no default.\n  - The commentary says delegation uses only `node_path`. This matches `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` in the same impl, which call `self.node_path(node)` and never edge discovery.\n  - The commentary says traversal fixtures separately exercise edge discovery. This holds: `impl[Memory/Domain]/fn[outgoing_edges]` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` returns real edges.\n- **Redundancy:** The item has no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to `habeas:coverage`, so the citation is not redundant.",
